      "side": 1,
      "message": "This change is just setting the ext4 block size to 4096 bytes, which might be increasing it from 1024 or it might be having no effect.  (mke2fs defaults to 1024-byte blocks for very small filesystems, and 4096-byte blocks otherwise.)  However, it does not change the dm-crypt sector size, which is 512 bytes by default.  Did you intend to increase the dm-crypt sector size instead of, or in addition, to this possible increase in the ext4 block size?\n\nAlso, it seems this code is using AES-HCTR2, not Adiantum.",
